  "database": "rschema_0511",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0511 database is designed to manage information about owners, employees, departments, and charges. The Owner_Table stores details about property owners, including their name, contact number, employer, house area, room number, and a unique identifier called Owner_ID. The Department_Table contains information about different departments, such as the department head, ID, name, and phone number, with a unique Department_ID serving as the primary key. The Employee_Table holds data about employees, including their address, contact number, date of birth, department ID, gender, name, password, position, and a unique Employee_ID. The Department_ID in the Employee_Table references the Department_ID in the Department_Table, establishing a relationship between employees and their departments. The Charge_Table tracks charges associated with specific rooms, owners, and employees, with columns for charge amount, date, type, employee ID, owner ID, quantity, and room number. The Charge_Table has a composite primary key consisting of the room number, owner ID, and charge date, ensuring each charge is unique. The Employee_ID and Owner_ID in the Charge_Table reference the Employee_ID and Owner_ID in the Employee_Table and Owner_Table, respectively, enforcing referential integrity by linking charges to the employees and owners responsible for them.",
  "gold_question": "System name: Community property fee management system\n\nDemand function description:\n1. Owner management:\nAdd owner record: record the basic information of the owner, including owner number, name, room number, house area, work unit, contact number, etc.\nQuery owner information: query the owner's information according to the room number.\n\n2. Department management:\nAdd department record: record the basic information of the department, including department number, department name, department head, department phone number, etc.\nQuery department information: query department information according to department number.\n\n3. Employee management:\nAdd employee record: record the basic information of employees, including employee number, name, date of birth, gender, address, contact number, department number, position and password, etc.\nQuery employee information: query employee information according to employee number.\nPermission management: employees can have different permissions according to their positions. Employees with the position of \"Manager\" can change the information of employees in this department, and employees with the position of \"Charge\" can only perform charging operations.\n\n4. Charge management:\nRecord charge information: including room number, owner number, charge date, charge type, quantity, charge amount, employee number, etc.\nGenerate charge slip: Generate charge slip based on charge information and record charge status.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0511.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0511\nCREATE TABLE `owner_table` (\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `employer` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `house_area` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `room_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`owner_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department_table` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_head` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_table` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department_table` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `charge_table` (\n  `room_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `charge_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `charge_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `charge_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`room_number`, `owner_id`, `charge_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `charge_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee_table` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `charge_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `owner_table` (`owner_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
